<h2>FAQ</h2>

<details><summary>Why do my wedding video highlights look flickering or strobing under decorative mandap LED stage lights?</summary>
<p>This optical artifact occurs when your camera's shutter speed (e.g., 1/50 or 1/60) is mathematically out of phase with the electrical frequency pulse of cheap third-party stage decor lights running on 50Hz Indian AC power grids! To eliminate flicker on sets: turn on **Synchro Scan or Variable Shutter Mode** inside your Sony or Panasonic camera menu, and fine-adjust shutter speeds by fractions of a decimal (e.g., 1/50.2 or 1/49.8) until monitor strobing instantly vanishes! In post-production, use DaVinci Resolve Studio's built-in **Deflicker OFX Plugin**.</p>
</details>

<details><summary>What is a Same-Day-Edit (SDE) at weddings and how on earth do editors pull it off?</summary>
<p>An SDE is an adrenaline-fueled production miracle where a dedicated on-site video editor cuts a 3-minute high-impact emotional wedding trailer from morning ceremony footage and screens it live on massive LED ballroom screens during the evening reception just hours later! It is achieved by having runner assistants hand over camera SD memory cards to an on-site MacBook workstation every two hours, utilizing pre-organized DaVinci project templates with pre-selected music beds and pre-built color grading node nodes.</p>
</details>

<details><summary>Should I deliver finished 4K wedding films to clients via physical Pen Drives or Cloud Links?</summary>
<p>Historically, Indian families loved decorative customized wooden USB flash drives in presentation boxes. Today, optical Flash NAND memory degrades over years, and modern thin laptops lack legacy USB-A ports! The contemporary industry best practice is delivering two digital pathways: a beautifully styled online interactive cloud viewing gallery (using tools like Vidflow, MediaZilla, or Google Drive folder structures) alongside an optional physical archival SSD or hard drive for lifetime safekeeping.</p>
</details>

<details><summary>How do I prevent my mirrorless camera from overheating and shutting off during a 3-hour non-stop Indian wedding ceremony in peak 42°C summer?</summary>
<p>Before shooting: enter your camera system hardware menu and set **Auto Power Off Temp to HIGH** (crucial for Sony users!). Never leave camera monitor LCD screens snapped shut flat against the overheating digital camera backplate—always swing out articulating screens to allow airflow! Shield camera bodies from direct overhead noon solar radiation using mini umbrellas or white gaffer tape, and carry dedicated cooling clip-on fans or dual external camera bodies to rotate during prolonged continuous homam rituals.</p>
</details>

